<title>FRANCE: Lille airport cargo traffic up 12 pct in October.</title>
<headline>Lille airport cargo traffic up 12 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lille-Lesquin Airport, in northern France, handled 2,396 tonnes of cargo traffic last month, up 12 percent on October 1995, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>In the first ten months of 1996, Lille Airport handled 20,179 tonnes of freight, an increase of nine percent on the same period last year.</p>
<p>Air France Europe and French handling agent, France Handling, KLM via its handling unit CSC and DHL, generate the most cargo traffic at Lille Airport. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
